{"name":"Diva Glam","hex":"#b24e76","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"diva","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any female celebrity, usually a well known singer or actress. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A person with an inflated sense of self, who has high expectations of others, and who is extremely demanding and fussy when it comes to personal privileges."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diva"},{"term":"glam","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Glamour; glamorousness.","Ellipsis of glam rock, the fashion and culture associated with this genre."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Glamorous."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glam"}],"entries":[{"title":"Diva","blocks":[{"text":"Diva, the Latin word for a goddess, has often been used as an honorific to refer to a celebrated woman of outstanding talent in the world of opera, theatre, cinema, fashion and popular music. If referring to an actress, the meaning of diva is closely related to that of prima donna. Diva can also refer to a person, especially one in show business, with a reputation for being temperamental or demanding. The application of the term has broadened beyond the performing arts to also include celebrated political and business figures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Mariah_Carey_-_Beautiful_%28Live_%40_GMA%2C_May_24%2C_2013%29.JPG/330px-Mariah_Carey_-_Beautiful_%28Live_%40_GMA%2C_May_24%2C_2013%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diva"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"diva":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/14/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-diva.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/1/14/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-diva.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng